# Never commit firmware images. A bootable ROM contains the Intel ME region
# and the flash descriptor from a specific machine -- proprietary, and
# carrying that machine's serial number, UUIDs and MAC address.
*.rom
*.bin
vendor/
readback*
console*.log
*.log

# ...except the blob-free release image, which has both of those regions
# erased to 0xFF and contains only our own coreboot build.
# (Consider attaching it as a GitHub Release asset instead of committing it.)
!release/mbp91-noblobs.rom

# Contains the hostname and MAC-address-shaped identifiers (see PUBLISHING.md).
notes/hardware-probe.txt
